<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Orosius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 375–after 418</span> · Also known as Paulus Orosius</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Orosius, or Paulus Orosius, was a Christian priest and historian from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Roman Hispania</a> and a pupil of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augustine-of-hippo">Augustine of Hippo</a>. His Seven Books of History against the Pagans, written around 417, surveys world history to argue that disasters had been worse before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>. Widely used as a textbook in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, it was translated into Old English in the reign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-the-great">Alfred the Great</a> with added geographical material.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/orosius.jpg" alt="Orosius" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paulo_Orosio_-_Detalle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
